:241.80837671981413,"t":567.66657954},"charspan":[0,46],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/6","text":""},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"where the values 0.59 nM and 0.007 nM are the values of emax and half-maximal effective concentration (EC50) respectively. This equation was fitted using human atrial myocyte  data  from  [11].  The  blocking  and  increasing factors were introduced to the ICaL, INa, IK1, and Ito equations in the cell model, as follows:","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":481.76461232272726,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":61.1999985,"r":297.03574421981426,"t":547.42100445},"charspan":[0,321],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/7","text":"where the values 0.59 nM and 0.007 nM are the values of emax and half-maximal effective concentration (EC50) respectively. This equation was fitted using human atrial myocyte  data  from  [11].  The  blocking  and  increasing factors were introduced to the ICaL, INa, IK1, and Ito equations in the cell model, as follows:"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"formula","orig":"𝐼 ஼௔௅ = ൫1 - 𝑏஼ை_஼௔௅ ൯(1 - 𝑏 ௌைమ_஼௔௅ )(1 + 𝑒ேை_஼௔௅ )𝑔 ஼௔௅ 𝑑𝑓𝑓 ஼௔ (𝑉 ௠ -65) , (9) 𝐼 ே௔ = ൫1 + 𝑒 ௌைమ_ே௔ ൯൫1 - 𝑏 ேை_ே௔ ൯𝑔 ே௔ 𝑚 ଷ ℎ𝑗(𝑉 ௠ 𝐸ே௔) ,           (10) 𝐼௄ଵ = (ଵ ା ௘ ೄೀ మ _಼భ )௚ ಼భ  (௏ ೘  ି ா ಼భ ) ଵ ା ௘ బ.బళ(ೇ శ ఴబ) ,         (10) 𝐼 ௧௢ = ൫1 + 𝑒 ௌைమ_௧௢ ൯𝑔௧௢ 𝑜𝑎 ଷ 𝑜𝑖(𝑉 ௠ -𝐸௧௢) ,           (11)","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":393.9581038457143,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":78.84000225,"r":290.8141146896284,"t":477.5007696},"charspan":[0,293],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/8","text":""},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"The modified model was incorporated into a 3D model of human atria to evaluate the dynamics of propagation.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":371.3646258227273,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":61.1999985,"r":296.7778310694296,"t":390.9409932},"charspan":[0,107],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/9","text":"The modified model was incorporated into a 3D model of human atria to evaluate the dynamics of propagation."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"2.2. 3D model of human atrial","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":346.1978085863637,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":61.1999985,"r":234.99189628303796,"t":356.04893580000004},"charspan":[0,29],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/10","text":"2.2. 3D model of human atrial"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"A 3D virtual model of human atria was implemented [12]. The model comprises the main anatomical structures, it  is  composed  of  515010  hexahedral  elements  with  a spatial  resolution  of  300  μm.  It  includes  realistic  fiber orientation, electrophysiological heterogeneity, and anisotropy.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":265.0446190727273,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":61.1999985,"r":296.8875581821785,"t":330.70098795},"charspan":[0,298],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/11","text":"A 3D virtual model of human atria was implemented [12]. The model comprises the main anatomical structures, it  is  composed  of  515010  hexahedral  elements  with  a spatial  resolution  of  300  μm.  It  includes  realistic  fiber orientation, electrophysiological heterogeneity, and anisotropy."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"To  simulate  the  cardiac  action  potential  propagation through the 3D model, the monodomain model described by the following reaction-diffusion equation was used:","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":230.48460557272733,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":61.1999985,"r":296.82246788548474,"t":261.70098795},"charspan":[0,166],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/12","text":"To  simulate  the  cardiac  action  potential  propagation through the 3D model, the monodomain model described by the following reaction-diffusion equation was used:"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"formula","orig":"ଵ ௌ ೡ ∇. (𝐷∇𝑉 ௠ ) = 𝐶 ௠ డ௏ ೘ డ௧ +𝐼௜௢௡ -𝐼௘௦௧ , (12)","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":209.94044933571433,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":90.60000225,"r":278.6271194396286,"t":228.06656604},"charspan":[0,50],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/13","text":""},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"where Vm is the transmembrane voltage, Cm is the specific membrane  capacitance  (100  pF),  Iion  is  the  total  ionic current  that  crosses  the  membrane,  Istim  is  the  stimulus current, Sv is the surface/volume ratio and D stands for the conductivity tensor. This equation was numerically solved using  the  finite  element  method  implemented  in  the EMOS® software, with a temporal resolution of 0.001 ms.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":131.24460032272736,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":61.1999985,"r":296.92023751349626,"t":208.42100445000005},"charspan":[0,418],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/14","text":"where Vm is the transmembrane voltage, Cm is the specific membrane  capacitance  (100  pF),  Iion  is  the  total  ionic current  that  crosses  the  membrane,  Istim  is  the  stimulus current, Sv is the surface/volume ratio and D stands for the conductivity tensor. This equation was numerically solved using  the  finite  element  method  implemented  in  the EMOS® software, with a temporal resolution of 0.001 ms."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"2.3. Simulation protocol","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":106.07782883636366,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":61.1999985,"r":201.5853580755831,"t":115.92895605000001},"charspan":[0,24],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/15","text":"2.3. Simulation protocol"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"For single-cell simulations, an S1-S1 stimulation protocol was applied, which consists of a train of rectangular  pulses  of  2  ms  duration  and  -2,000  pA  to generate action potentials at a base cycle length (BCL) of 1000 ms. The APD at 90% of the repolarization (APD90) and the different currents were measured on the 10th beat.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":82.40460407272735,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":72.71999925,"r":296.8034604678669,"t":90.58100820000004},"charspan":[0,49],"page_no":1},{"bbox":{"b":663.0846078227273,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":317.51998875,"r":553.30523625,"t":717.2210059500001},"charspan":[50,334],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/16","text":"For single-cell simulations, an S1-S1 stimulation protocol was applied, which consists of a train of rectangular  pulses  of  2  ms  duration  and  -2,000  pA  to generate action potentials at a base cycle length (BCL) of 1000 ms. The APD at 90% of the repolarization (APD90) and the different currents were measured on the 10th beat."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"To simulate arrhythmias in the 3D model, an S1-S2-S3 stimulation protocol was applied, where S1 simulates the sinus rhythm as a train of stimuli applied in the sinoatrial node at a BCL of 500 ms. S2 and S3 simulate two ectopic foci  composed  of  6  stimuli  each.  S2  is  located  at  the interatrial  septum  near  the  coronary  sinus  and  S3  at  the posterior wall of the left  atrium, in the base of the right pulmonary  veins.  The  first  S2  and  S3  were  applied  at coupling  intervals  that  generated  a  unidirectional  block, with cycle lengths selected such that the second stimulus from each focus also generated a unidirectional block. The simulations ran for 5 seconds. To calculate the number of reentries, reentry is defined as the propagation activity that presents 2 or more consecutive turns.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":502.0445958227273,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":317.51998875,"r":555.6664173753621,"t":659.74101195},"charspan":[0,819],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/17","text":"To simulate arrhythmias in the 3D model, an S1-S2-S3 stimulation protocol was applied, where S1 simulates the sinus rhythm as a train of stimuli applied in the sinoatrial node at a BCL of 500 ms. S2 and S3 simulate two ectopic foci  composed  of  6  stimuli  each.  S2  is  located  at  the interatrial  septum  near  the  coronary  sinus  and  S3  at  the posterior wall of the left  atrium, in the base of the right pulmonary  veins.  The  first  S2  and  S3  were  applied  at coupling  intervals  that  generated  a  unidirectional  block, with cycle lengths selected such that the second stimulus from each focus also generated a unidirectional block. The simulations ran for 5 seconds. To calculate the number of reentries, reentry is defined as the propagation activity that presents 2 or more consecutive turns."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Table  1  shows  the  concentrations  defined  for  each polluting gas, where the high concentration corresponds to an approximate value of the IC50, the medium is half of the high concentration and the low corresponds to 20% of the high concentration.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":444.5646078227272,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":317.51998875,"r":553.2115402970563,"t":498.70101120000004},"charspan":[0,252],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/18","text":"Table  1  shows  the  concentrations  defined  for  each polluting gas, where the high concentration corresponds to an approximate value of the IC50, the medium is half of the high concentration and the low corresponds to 20% of the high concentration."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"caption","orig":"Table 1. Gaseous air pollutants concentrations.","parent":{"$ref":"#/tables/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":421.6446093227272,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":317.51998875,"r":507.3241295527399,"t":429.82101345},"charspan":[0,47],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/19","text":"Table 1. Gaseous air pollutants concentrations."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"3. Results","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":312.23783258636365,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":317.51998875,"r":393.7314831534495,"t":322.0889598},"charspan":[0,10],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/20","text":"3. Results"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"The  results  of  single-cell  simulations  indicate  that individual gaseous pollutants exhibit pro-arrhythmic effects  in  a  concentration-dependent  manner  by  altering the action potential.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":254.00459507272728,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":317.51998875,"r":553.1380384119336,"t":296.74101195000003},"charspan":[0,195],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/21","text":"The  results  of  single-cell  simulations  indicate  that individual gaseous pollutants exhibit pro-arrhythmic effects  in  a  concentration-dependent  manner  by  altering the action potential."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Under  healthy  conditions,  as  the  CO  concentration increased, a reduction in the magnitude of the maximum peak of the ICaL current was observed and consequently, a reduction in APD90 of 23.6% (Figure 1A).","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":208.0446190727273,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":317.51998875,"r":553.237252121807,"t":250.78099020000002},"charspan":[0,209],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/22","text":"Under  healthy  conditions,  as  the  CO  concentration increased, a reduction in the magnitude of the maximum peak of the ICaL current was observed and consequently, a reduction in APD90 of 23.6% (Figure 1A)."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"As the SO2 concentration increased, APD90 was reduced up  to  38.8%,  also  presenting  a  loss  of  the  dome  of  the plateau phase (Figure 1B). The above is a consequence of the  alterations  in  the  ionic  currents,  which  include  a reduction in the magnitude of the maximum peak of the ICaL current, and an increase in the maximum peaks of the INa, Ito, and IK1 currents.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":127.52458382272732,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":317.51998875,"r":553.240593612749,"t":204.70098795},"charspan":[0,379],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/23","text":"As the SO2 concentration increased, APD90 was reduced up  to  38.8%,  also  presenting  a  loss  of  the  dome  of  the plateau phase (Figure 1B). The above is a consequence of the  alterations  in  the  ionic  currents,  which  include  a reduction in the magnitude of the maximum peak of the ICaL current, and an increase in the maximum peaks of the INa, Ito, and IK1 currents."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Finally, as the NOx concentration increased, an increase in the magnitude of the maximum peak of the INa and ICaL currents  was  observed,  an  effect  opposite  to  what  was observed in  the  other  two  gases.  This  generated  a  more","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":81.56460782272734,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":317.51998875,"r":553.285293,"t":124.18099919999997},"charspan":[0,238],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/24","text":"Finally, as the NOx concentration increased, an increase in the magnitude of the maximum peak of the INa and ICaL currents  was  observed,  an  effect  opposite  to  what  was observed in  the  other  two  gases.  This  generated  a  more"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"furniture","label":"page_footer","orig":"Page 2","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":35.369998099999975,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":290.755,"r":321.24593450000003,"t":45.177279},"charspan":[0,6],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/25","text":"Page 2"}],"version":"1.10.0"}